80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Go's database/sql and pgx provide a clear API for transactions. The most important practice is using defer tx.Rollback\(\). If your function returns early due to an error, the rollback is triggered automatically. If you call tx.Commit\(\), the rollback becomes a "no-op," ensuring your data is safe either way.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
