/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (A deadlock occurs when Transaction A holds a lock on Row 1 and wants Row 2, while Transaction B holds Row 2 and wants Row 1. Neither can move. Postgres will eventually detect this and kill one of them, but it's better to avoid it entirely.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
